/* the hidden layer */
L.hid={
 title:'Finer details',
 face:{
  Mars:'This part of the sign is coloured by Mars, so it has an edge: more drive, quicker reactions, a readiness to fight for it.',
  Sun:'This part of the sign is coloured by the Sun, so it wants to be seen, to lead and to be proud of itself.',
  Venus:'This part of the sign is coloured by Venus, so it softens towards beauty, pleasure, charm and harmony.',
  Mercury:'This part of the sign is coloured by Mercury, so it gets clever: more talk, more analysis, more nerves.',
  Moon:'This part of the sign is coloured by the Moon, so it becomes more emotional, receptive and changeable.',
  Saturn:'This part of the sign is coloured by Saturn, so it is more serious, patient and ready to work, and a little shy.',
  Jupiter:'This part of the sign is coloured by Jupiter, so it is more generous, hopeful and expansive, and sometimes too much.'},
 deg:{
  fresh:'It sits at the very start of the sign, so this energy is new and raw, like someone in their first week at a new job: eager, a bit clumsy, all potential.',
  late:'It sits in the last degrees of the sign, where the sign is wise, a little tired and already glancing at the next one.',
  anaretic:'It sits at 29°, the last degree of the sign, which astrologers call the anaretic degree. It often feels urgent, as if this planet has unfinished business and wants to get it right in this life.'},
 sect:{
  day:'You were born by day (the Sun above the horizon), so your chart is a day chart.',
  night:'You were born at night (the Sun below the horizon), so your chart is a night chart.',
  Jupiter:{in:'In a day chart Jupiter is your most helpful planet: its gifts arrive more easily and more reliably. Where it sits is where life tends to be generous to you.',out:'In a night chart Jupiter still helps, but less loudly. Venus is the one that does the heavy lifting for you.'},
  Venus:{in:'In a night chart Venus is your most helpful planet: love, beauty and pleasure tend to rescue you more than effort does.',out:'In a day chart Venus helps, but Jupiter is your main helper. Venus works best when you ask for what you want instead of waiting.'},
  Saturn:{in:'In a day chart Saturn behaves itself: its lessons are hard but fair, and discipline pays off.',out:'In a night chart Saturn is your most difficult planet. Its lessons can feel cold or unfair, and they are also where you grow most.'},
  Mars:{in:'In a night chart Mars is calmer and more useful: its fire warms rather than burns.',out:'In a day chart Mars is the most difficult planet: it runs hot, rushes and picks fights. It is also where your greatest courage comes from, once it has a worthy target.'}},
 sun:{
  cazimi:'This planet is cazimi, "in the heart of the Sun": within a few minutes of exact conjunction. Traditionally that is a huge honour, like being invited into the king\'s chamber. Whatever it rules gets the Sun\'s full backing.',
  combust:'This planet is combust: so close to the Sun that it is lost in its glare. Traditionally that means it is hard to see clearly, even for you. In practice its themes merge with your identity: you do not have a mind (or heart, or drive), you are it. Hard to step back from, and very personal.',
  beams:'This planet is under the Sun\'s beams: close enough to be partly hidden. It works in the background, behind your identity, and often comes out in its own time.'},
 star:{
  Mercury:{m:'Your Mercury rose before the Sun on the day you were born, a "morning" Mercury. Traditionally that is a mind that jumps ahead: fast, forward-looking, eager to speak first.',e:'Your Mercury set after the Sun, an "evening" Mercury. Traditionally that is a reflective mind that thinks things over and understands afterwards, with deep hindsight.'},
  Venus:{m:'Your Venus was the morning star at your birth, Lucifer, the light-bringer. Traditionally that is a bold, active, impulsive way of loving that goes after what it wants.',e:'Your Venus was the evening star at your birth, Hesperus, the one that comes out at dusk. Traditionally that is a receptive, romantic, sensual way of loving that is drawn in rather than chasing.'}},
 station:'This planet was almost standing still at your birth (stationary). A stationary planet is very powerful: its energy is concentrated, like a held breath, and it becomes a major theme of your life.',
 dig:{
  digHome:'At home: this planet is in a sign it rules, so it speaks its native language. It does not need permission and it does not need explaining.',
  digExalt:'Exalted: like an honoured guest, this planet is treated beautifully here and shows its best side, sometimes a bit idealised.',
  digDet:'In detriment: this planet is living abroad, in the sign opposite its home. It still works; it just works in a foreign language. People with planets in detriment often become unusually skilled at those themes, because nothing came automatically.',
  digFall:'In fall: this planet sits opposite the sign where it is honoured, so its gifts are less obvious and need patience. Planets in fall tend to become wise rather than easy.',
  both:'In detriment and in fall at the same time: as far from home as a planet can be. That sounds like bad news and usually is not. It means you had to build this part of yourself from scratch, and what you build from scratch you understand better than anyone born with it.'},
 abroadP:{
  Sun:'Your sense of self does not run on the spotlight. It runs on something larger than you, which makes you less selfish than most and sometimes less sure of yourself.',
  Moon:'Comfort was something you had to build rather than something you were simply given, so you know exactly how it is made.',
  Mercury:'Your mind does not work like the textbook. It works by image, mood and intuition, and it gets to the answer by a road nobody else can follow, then has to find the words afterwards.',
  Venus:'You love in a style the romance novels never prepared anyone for: direct, impatient, brave. It took time to learn that being wanted and being cherished are different things, and that you deserve both.',
  Mars:'Your fight is not automatic. It is slow, chosen and stubborn, which makes it far harder to stop once it has started.',
  Jupiter:'Your luck is not the lottery kind. It arrives through careful, specific effort, and then it stays.',
  Saturn:'Your discipline had to make friends with something soft (feelings, or pride, or play), so your rules are more human than most.'},
 abroad:n=>`${["","One","Two","Three","Four","Five","Six","Seven"][n]||n} of your planets are in detriment or fall, living abroad in signs that do not come naturally to them. That is unusual. It is not a curse: it is the chart of someone who had to learn by doing what other people got for free, which tends to produce depth, empathy and a lot of improvised skill. You may have felt slightly out of step with the world. That out-of-step quality is also what makes you interesting.`,
 rulerIn:[
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 1st house, so your life is shaped mostly by your own choices and your own presence.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 2nd house, so your life is steered by what you value and what you build with your own hands.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 3rd house, so your life is steered by learning, words and the people close to you.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 4th house, so your life is steered from the roots: home, family and a private inner base.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 5th house, so your life is steered by joy, love and creative self-expression.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 6th house, so your life is steered by work, skill and the daily craft of being useful.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 7th house, so your life is steered through other people: partners, mirrors and collaborators.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 8th house, and that is a big clue to your whole life. The planet that represents you lives in the house of depth, intimacy, crisis and other people\'s secrets. So however bright you look, a lot of your life happens in close bonds, big changes and things you do not post online. You were made to go through things, not around them.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 9th house, so your life is steered by meaning, travel and the search for truth.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 10th house, so your life is steered by your calling and your public role.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 11th house, so your life is steered by friends, groups and the future you believe in.',
  'Your chart ruler sits in the 12th house, so your life is steered from backstage: solitude, intuition and inner life.']
};

